ments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:50:23-07:00","id":290828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=290459#post290459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't have clearance to spoil the actual Dominance Facets themselves, but I could talk a bit about my thinking behind the new Dominance design if you want, albeit it'll be a bit vague <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point we will greedily consume anything a writer or a developer, who was involved in this project, posts, even if it is only vaguely related to the new edition. <i>The delay is getting to us...</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:29:43-07:00","id":290843,"title":"","content":"NDAs are srs bsns but there gotta be a way to allow to make 'em a lil bit more flexible in these instances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T07:20:24-07:00","id":291319,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ebD2r-8vo8Y\" target=\"_blank\">Swap &quot;open, open, open&quot; for &quot;publish, publish, publish&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T09:01:35-07:00","id":291390,"title":"","content":"Is there any planned change to origins of Werewolves in 2ed? I want to write up my own version of Gaia soonish (she did not create Werewolves, though) and have Luna as her firstborn daughter, so I feel obliged to include Werewolves in the context of the write-up and ask if core 1ed stuff is still more or less kosher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T09:13:14-07:00","id":291396,"title":"","content":"You could always have done that, Gaea hasn't really been explored in World of Darkness yet but I think Mr Brookshaw did some take on it, as well as Helios.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T09:20:39-07:00","id":291406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could always have done that, Gaea hasn't really been explored in World of Darkness yet but I think Mr Brookshaw did some take on it, as well as Helios. </div> </div> </div>My Gaia take is vastly different from one may know from OWoD. Rank 9 planetary Celestine as old as planet itself which is embodiment of evolution and survival of the fittest. Not nicest Celestine around, I'll say, given some of her harsh methods to foster evolutionary change (including technological, technology is valid to her if it stems from ingenuity of species).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T09:51:13-07:00","id":291426,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty appropriate for the nWoD setting. I don't have much experience with oWoD so I wouldn't really be able to tell.<br /> <br /> There -is- a Gaea (as in Pangaea) but its been mentioned twice in all the books I have, like a sentence each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2014, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T10:16:10-07:00","id":291441,"title":"","content":"So far I involved her in Vampire (created first Gangrel to prey on humans and keep their survival instincts sharp) and Changeling (let Gentry enter Earth, as before they could only kidnap mortals straying into Hedge, but as the payment she levied on them weakness to iron, metal associated with. Motivation was that as she lets them be a danger to humans they should face challenge as well. She finds them boring because lack of creativity, but again they are useful for her agenda, so it's just business).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T10:48:34-07:00","id":291454,"title":"","content":"Cool. I like the tie in with the gangrel. What are your plans for it in Werewolf, aside from being mother of Luna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2014, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T11:53:23-07:00","id":291473,"title":"","content":"Here's something I'd like to hear Dave Brookshaw weigh in on: Is there clarification on where Essence comes from? GMC indicates that actions and emotions in the material world generate it and spirits gain it when they are in resonant areas (which I kind of view as current being generated in a wire in a magnetic field because physics major). But does that mean that you won't find Essence resonant with mountains, cars, etc outside of a spirit of that sort? Since a mountain is neither an activity nor an emotion? Just something I always wanted clarification on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:03:31-07:00","id":291478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool. I like the tie in with the gangrel. What are your plans for it in Werewolf, aside from being mother of Luna? </div> </div> </div>I read up on the backstory in the core already and here is my preliminary draft:<br /> <br /> At first She was proud of her daughter Luna's relationship with Father Wolf. She approved of Pangea where her son-in-law and grandchildren ruled as mighty predators with sheer prowess. But Father Wolf grew weak. Pangea started to become paradise for those humans who allied with spirits that leaked in. At first she had low expectations of the ape, but they developed tools to compensate for their weakness and even were bold enough to try and resist the rule of werewolves, so she look curiously at humans. No way she would let such potentially promising creatures stagnate because of Father Wolf's weakness. It is unclear if she subtly spurred would be Forsaken in action and certainly erecting Gauntlet was not in her plans as it partly diminished her influence as well. But the murder of Father Wolf impressed her as much as when one of those humans killed his brother with a sharpened stone. She is after all, among many other things, a spirit that embodies conflict. Humans later on developed to be more interesting in her eyes than her grandchildren that she used to favor (symbolically, as a rule she provides no supernatural boons unless they carry some potent drawback), but conflict between Forsaken and Pure is not dull and if humans get into crossfire that may make them stronger.<br /> <br /> Probably spirits that fall into her domain are representations of ambition, conflict, change, evolution (genetic and memetic as well), natural disasters and plagues. Given that Forsaken are meant to keep balance between spirit and material world, they might clash with Gaia's spirits if they flock to rage and strife like moths to light.<br /> <br /> If an Urathra is willing to accept a boon for a steep price they might seek service under one of Gaia's avatars. One of them I had mind is ironically not unlike Hircine from Elder Scrolls. But with boobs if I keep Gaia's gender consistent for all avatars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-24-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:09:07-07:00","id":291482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=291473#post291473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something I'd like to hear Dave Brookshaw weigh in on: Is there clarification on where Essence comes from? GMC indicates that actions and emotions in the material world generate it and spirits gain it when they are in resonant areas (which I kind of view as current being generated in a wire in a magnetic field because physics major). But does that mean that you won't find Essence resonant with mountains, cars, etc outside of a spirit of that sort? Since a mountain is neither an activity nor an emotion? Just something I always wanted clarification on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emotion <i>and memory</i> are the two main things that are called out as generating Essence (hence ghosts), and the bulk of &quot;natural&quot; distortion of the Shadow is a consequence of a surfeit of a given perspective - hence why so many rivers seem deeper, mountains seem taller, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:49:52-07:00","id":291514,"title":"","content":"I'm also interested in how the cosmology might have changed with Luna and Sol. As I remember talk of them being made into fulcrums of the Spirit Realm and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:56:41-07:00","id":291519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=291478#post291478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read up on the backstory in the core already and here is my preliminary draft:<br /> <br /> At first She was proud of her daughter Luna's relationship with Father Wolf. She approved of Pangea where her son-in-law and grandchildren ruled as mighty predators with sheer prowess. But Father Wolf grew weak. Pangea started to become paradise for those humans who allied with spirits that leaked in. At first she had low expectations of the ape, but they developed tools to compensate for their weakness and even were bold enough to try and resist the rule of werewolves, so she look curiously at humans. No way she would let such potentially promising creatures stagnate because of Father Wolf's weakness. It is unclear if she subtly spurred would be Forsaken in action and certainly erecting Gauntlet was not in her plans as it partly diminished her influence as well. But the murder of Father Wolf impressed her as much as when one of those humans killed his brother with a sharpened stone. She is after all, among many other things, a spirit that embodies conflict. Humans later on developed to be more interesting in her eyes than her grandchildren that she used to favor (symbolically, as a rule she provides no supernatural boons unless they carry some potent drawback), but conflict between Forsaken and Pure is not dull and if humans get into crossfire that may make them stronger.<br /> <br /> Probably spirits that fall into her domain are representations of ambition, conflict, change, evolution (genetic and memetic as well), natural disasters and plagues. Given that Forsaken are meant to keep balance between spirit and material world, they might clash with Gaia's spirits if they flock to rage and strife like moths to light.<br /> <br /> If an Urathra is willing to accept a boon for a steep price they might seek service under one of Gaia's avatars. One of them I had mind is ironically not unlike Hircine from Elder Scrolls. But with boobs if I keep Gaia's gender consistent for all avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of giving such omnipresent deities anything resembling coherence or logic in it's actions, even if they could be tracked back to a single entity. Not merely because it's a deity but because spirits are meant to be alien. A spirit which embodies death by fire doesn't causes misery because of a notion of amusement, but because it simply is, for example - could kill with boiling water or with merely a fever. In contrast, a spirit of controlled or confined fire breaks out, that got a taste for the freedom it had never tasted before would be as explosive. Any humans caught in the blast are merely the ants that construct the receptacles for more thrills, or innocent bystanders.<br /> <br /> Take a look at how Luna's been portrayed, or rather, how she hasn't. She doesn't confers audience. Her will is made known thru omens and her servants, and the later could very well be actually like any other spirit's agenda for all the Uratha know. All they have to go on about is legends and faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 10-24-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:04:08-07:00","id":291524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not a fan of giving such omnipresent deities anything resembling coherence or logic in it's actions, even if they could be tracked back to a single entity. Not merely because it's a deity but because spirits are meant to be alien. A spirit which embodies death by fire doesn't causes misery because of a notion of amusement, but because it simply is, for example - could kill with boiling water or with merely a fever. In contrast, a spirit of controlled or confined fire breaks out, that got a taste for the freedom it had never tasted before would be as explosive. Any humans caught in the blast are merely the ants that construct the receptacles for more thrills, or innocent bystanders.<br /> <br /> Take a look at how Luna's been portrayed, or rather, how she hasn't. She doesn't confers audience. Her will is made known thru omens and her servants, and the later could very well be actually like any other spirit's agenda for all the Uratha know. All they have to go on about is legends and faith. </div> </div> </div>That could have been as well case of our mortal minds anthromorphising such beings in order to better cope with them. Think of me as a subjective observer whose mind cannot comprehend truly the Celestine so gives logic and coherence to whatever it does. I also channel a bit from Warhammer. Surely Ruinous Powers are concepts and emotions made manifest, but they have personalities ascribed to them.<br /> <br /> Whatever I shall write about Gaia may be my slanted view that tries to ascribe meaning to something beyond manifest conception. And maybe I'm also insane. It's your choice if you pick such characterisation, and I may as well provide alternate take that compares Gaia to a principle. And both takes may be wrong, who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-24-2014, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:28:33-07:00","id":291538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=291482#post291482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emotion <i>and memory</i> are the two main things that are called out as generating Essence (hence ghosts), and the bulk of &quot;natural&quot; distortion of the Shadow is a consequence of a surfeit of a given perspective - hence why so many rivers seem deeper, mountains seem taller, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The major difference between the deep wilderness Shadow and the deep Urban Shadow is how much prominence non-human lives shape it - animals and plants create Essence as well.<br /> <br /> I don't think we mention Gaea anywhere outside of Rank charts in books and material building from them, where it's always said to be a theoretical entity one Rank above Luna and Helios, but no one's ever managed to talk to it and it doesn't create Royal Avatars. So it might not exist at all.<br /> <br /> (Note that, despite it being spelled wrong in a couple of books, it's <b>Gaea</b> in the nWoD, not <b>Gaia</b>.)<br /> <br /> Helios has always been around in Forsaken, just kinda bubbling under. We've done a lot in second edition to pin down just what Wolf, Luna, and Helios are spirits <i>of</i>, which involved clarifying Wolf and Luna a bit and giving Helios a purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:57:12-07:00","id":291552,"title":"","content":"I've been reading this book, Autobiography of a Werewolf Hunter. It's fantastic, and I'd be surprised if it wasn't influenced a bit by World of Darkness, though the werewolves (the readers have seen) are much more diabolical. &quot;the devil for a father, the moon for a mother.&quot;<br /> <br /> I must admit, it's been nice to some extent not really knowing about Father Wolf, as it gives more veracity to the 'blasphemies' that might suggest things aren't exactly like the stories that have been passed down thousands of years suggest.<br /> <br /> Malcolm Sheppard had <a href=\"https://mobunited.wordpress.com/2012/09/21/a-half-baked-werewolf-the-forsaken-reboot-pitch/\" target=\"_blank\">a nice take on the whole thing</a> too, in the interest of origins. Apparently no matter how powerful they are or influential if it's a spirit, to the community, it's 'just a spirit.' It'd be nice to shed that perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2014, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:30:45-07:00","id":291573,"title":"","content":"I took into account in my emerging write-up that anthromorphisation of Gaia (also known as The World and Kybele, among other countless names) might be how our subjective minds try to give form to what is beyond comprehension, and first described her in more general terms as hypothetical singular Celestine that reflects the world itself, including all lifeforms, a cycle of life, death and rebirth, Earth in its all glory and horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:40:38-07:00","id":291619,"title":"","content":"Yeah that could certainly fit into things as they are, though I'd be curious as to how much the players would know about the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T18:46:05-07:00","id":291739,"title":"","content":"Katsura, you're making me want to do a Cosmology megathread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=291538#post291538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helios has always been around in Forsaken, just kinda bubbling under. We've done a lot in second edition to pin down just what Wolf, Luna, and Helios are spirits <i>of</i>, which involved clarifying Wolf and Luna a bit and giving Helios a purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about this stuff. I always thought the Celestial spirits were interesting concepts, but besides Luna and a few blurbs on Helios/Sol, we never heard too much about them.<br /> <br /> Same with Father Wolf, actually. I have my own theories, but more ideas on what exactly that thing's deal is are always nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T02:07:35-07:00","id":291883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Katsura, you're making me want to do a Cosmology megathread. </div> </div> </div>Please do. It will be interesting, I think.<br /> <br /> And BTW, my write up is already 300 words long, though far from completion and have to juggle between:<br /> <br /> 1) Preparing for today's session of Vampire Masquerade (I would prefer Requiem at this point, but I'm fine with Masquerade too)<br /> 2) Making a Changeling character for a crossover RP (It's a crossover that can include any franchise, on conditions that power level cap is not exceeded. And technically no aliens). I took a character from Fate/Apocrypha and plan to make her Changeling version.<br /> 3) Designing the Changeling's former Keeper. He will be twisted reflection of Arthurian legends and other chivalric myths. Ego rivalling Fate Stay Night's Gilgamesh.<br /> 4) Doing some of work related stuff for Tuesday. Pecunia non olet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T08:24:39-07:00","id":292043,"title":"","content":"What are the perks of becoming Wolf-Blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T08:26:13-07:00","id":292044,"title":"","content":"I've been looking forward to a bigger part for Helios. Any chance we might see some gift aspects that come from Helios? 1st edition made mention in Predators that Luna put some of the most powerful gifts in the care of Helios and that he doesn't give them up because the wolves killed his Sister's lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:42:03-07:00","id":292264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292043#post292043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the perks of becoming Wolf-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a few different things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\">Check out the blog post about them.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name"