.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292379#post292379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the part in the blog post where it talks about having eight tells worked out?<br /> <br /> The final book has <i>twenty-seven</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know how to sweet talk an audience, don't you Stew? Can't wait. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T16:52:56-07:00","id":292513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292379#post292379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the part in the blog post where it talks about having eight tells worked out?<br /> <br /> The final book has <i>twenty-seven</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you do this to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:45:47-07:00","id":292583,"title":"","content":"Because he loves to see you, and everyone, twist in the wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:41:17-07:00","id":292885,"title":"","content":"I'll write up some of the ideas behind the new Dominance approach when I get home later today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292044#post292044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking forward to a bigger part for Helios. Any chance we might see some gift aspects that come from Helios? 1st edition made mention in Predators that Luna put some of the most powerful gifts in the care of Helios and that he doesn't give them up because the wolves killed his Sister's lover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to do a Gift of the Sun but there wasn't space to put new Gifts into the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292304#post292304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to be, yes. Someone thinks there'll be rites to transform wolf-blooded into werewolves.<br /> <br /> Either way it does seem better than the genetic option.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't technically a rite to turn wolf-blooded into werewolves, but there are some rites that... blur some lines on the human -&gt; wolf-blooded -&gt; werewolf scale a bit. Or a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292379#post292379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the part in the blog post where it talks about having eight tells worked out?<br /> <br /> The final book has <i>twenty-seven</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit to being hugely impressed when I first read the Wolf-Blooded section draft and realising just <i>how</i> <i>much </i>content had been crammed in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292513#post292513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you do this to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>The man's a menace, and must be stopped! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T12:47:38-07:00","id":293129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292885#post292885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't technically a rite to turn wolf-blooded into werewolves, but there are some rites that... blur some lines on the human -&gt; wolf-blooded -&gt; werewolf scale a bit. Or a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, glad to hear it. From the looks of it Werewolves have a lot more to sort of force them into dealing with people and wolf-blooded, that's a good thing and I think a better option than just being able to turn them into werewolves and send them on their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-26-2014, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:25:16-07:00","id":293163,"title":"","content":"So, those thoughts about the Dominance Gift...<br /> <br /> The 1st edition Dominance Gift list had the much-maligned targeting restrictions, but it was also already rather narrowly focused. Three powers that amount to 'shout at someone to get them to do A Thing', one minor defensive buff and one to strip Willpower off a target. What you could inflict on a target with the command Gifts was extremely limited until you got to the fifth dot. Low-dot Dominance was also extremely costly to use due to being fuelled off Willpower. To me, it was an underwhelming Gift list until the 4th dot, providing an overly complex system for achieving relatively minor control capabilities over very limited periods of time.<br /> <br /> So, when looking at redoing Dominance for 2nd edition, I knew I wanted to significantly change the Gift up.<br /> <br /> Before setting to work on the 2nd edition Gifts, I spent some time mulling over the new Blood &amp; Smoke Discipline write-ups. It was useful to gauge what sort of changes had been made, how they had been empowered, and what stuff vampires had that I specifically <i>didn't</i> want to then cover with Gifts. I knew already that I didn't want Dominance to just be Werewolf Dominate and, as I read over them, it was clear that the vampiric 'social' Disciplines do a particular thing where they offer an end-run round the social system. A Ventrue with Dominate or a Daeva with Majesty just twists a victim's mind like a pretzel. For the Gift of Dominance, I wanted something that took a different approach - to have at least some of its Facets work within the new social manoeuver system rather than bulldozing over it.<br /> <br /> To lay out the obvious, Dominance should be about asserting dominance, not about mind control.<br /> <br /> I went through the existing Dominance Gifts to see what I might want to keep and what to get rid of. Warning Growl - a low worth combat boost that's basically a speed-bump. Combat Dominance should be about putting the other guy or girl right in their place with a display of power, not making them a bit nervous. <i>Cut</i>. Luna's Dictum, Voice of Command and Tug the Soul's Strings - just ascending forms of a command power that take a massive amount of word count for little worth, and I don't want such blatant 'mind control' in the new Gift with all the accompanying verbage and wrangling about what you can and can't do; I'm happy for that to remain more of a vampire thing. <i>Cut.</i> Break the Defiant - the only one I actually seriously think about keeping, but for various reasons to do with Willpower in the new edition I decide it's better off gone. <i>Cut.</i><br /> <br /> So... having at this point decided I'm binning the entire existing mechanical structure for Dominance, I have to rebuild it. With 2nd edition, there's the added wrinkle that there need to be five distinct powers that are not inter-reliant, each reflecting a different Renown and each as viable as the others - they don't all need to be specifically balanced in 'power' compared to one another, but they all need to be <i>desirable</i> to at least some characters.<br /> <br /> When I sit down and sketch out what I have in mind for new Facets, some are straightforward and come quickly to mind. Two that are enhancements that work within the existing social manoeuver system - one for the alluring and sexy predator or the charming wolf-in-sheep's clothing, an easy fit for Cunning, and one for the dominating, snarling in-your-face werewolf that slots into Purity nicely. Both help you get what you want, but they're both short-term. The Cunning Facet works smoothly as long as you don't push the prey too hard and make them realise your true nature; Purity just goes full speed ahead, damn the torpedoes and any consequences of getting what you want right now. With the former, they might never know they were even prey; with the latter, there's no mistaking their place in the chain of dominance.<br /> <br /> I knew I wanted a solid combat-useable Facet that lent itself to the sort of physical challenges that Uratha tend towards - a genuine social<i> attack</i>, dominance through raw violence. Assert your superiority through <i>hammering the other guy's head against the wall</i>. Into Honor this one goes.<br /> <br /> Thing is, Dominance Through Violence (or, as the Facet is actually called, Lay Low The Challenger) might seem to fit better in Glory - and I do have a system for how I place Facets in given Renowns - but in this case, I had two solid reasons for it going into Honor. One is that it does serve as a tool - a violent tool - for asserting position and status within pack organisation; the other is that I already knew what I was going to put into Glory. Some Facets play around with Lunacy, custom-tailoring it, and I had one in mind for Dominance. After figuring out exactly what it did, it was obvious that Glory was the slot for it.<br /> <br /> One left - Wisdom. A few possibilities here, but some crossed over too closely into Inspiration territory. In the end I went for something a bit different - a more beneficial take on dominance, one that fiddles with the boundaries of the pack and is more about allies than intimidation.<br /> <br /> Five Facets in place, then; Purity is the closest to the old Dominance powers, but the whole Gift gives several tools for approaching social situations, violence and the pack. The most niche is probably the Wisdom Facet, but that's ok - there are still characters for whom it is a solid choice, especially as it offers some serious synergy with other Gifts and Rites.<br /> <br /> So, I go over the list again, tweak it, adjust powers, make things a bit more streamlined. The Purity Facet gets a dice roll element removed so that it just gives the benefit if the price is paid. The effects of Lay Low The Challenger get modified several times as I seek the right balance so that it isn't just a no-brainer combat choice for every werewolf, but remains an actively useful tool in both violence and social actions. Glory gets poked with a stick a bit but basically does what I want it to do quite well. I've torn out the old Dominance limitations on targets, and nothing in rewriting or playtesting makes me feel like there's any reason to put it back in.<br /> <br /> End result - a Gift of Dominance that has none of the old powers in it but, to my mind, offers the key features of what dominance <i>should</i> include - not control via carefully chosen words and directions but rather power through violence, through raw force of personality, through sex and through glorious terror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:56:56-07:00","id":293229,"title":"","content":"I do have to wonder why <i>27</i> tells are included. Surely even a dozen would be enough and the word-count could've gone to other things, while the remaining tells could be saved for a supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T15:30:56-07:00","id":293240,"title":"","content":"Given the expanded role of wolf-blooded and the removal of the restrictions on werewolves inter-breeding, I'm very happy to have so many tells. It keeps wolf-blooded from being, essentially, eight splats. Instead, they really will come across as wild cards, with a broad range of possible talents and limitations so you are never sure what you are dealing with when you go up against a new one. Much more fitting for those touched by a mad god/dess of change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T15:51:57-07:00","id":293248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=293163#post293163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">End result - a Gift of Dominance that has none of the old powers in it but, to my mind, offers the key features of what dominance <i>should</i> include - not control via carefully chosen words and directions but rather power through violence, through raw force of personality, <b>through sex </b>and through glorious terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, finally seduction is a viable way to interact with humans...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T18:52:39-07:00","id":293341,"title":"","content":"You also have to remember that Tells are in the Merit section for the Wolf-Blooded. So they have pretty small word counts anyway. Its why Hurt Locker and Secrets of the Covenants has large amounts of them. They usually only require about 3-6 sentences and reference something else. So you can easily toss out a ton of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T04:03:31-07:00","id":293622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=292044#post292044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking forward to a bigger part for Helios. Any chance we might see some gift aspects that come from Helios? 1st edition made mention in Predators that Luna put some of the most powerful gifts in the care of Helios and that he doesn't give them up because the wolves killed his Sister's lover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so - and that's unfortunately why they'd be reserved for apocryphal material. I could see an individual Pack or a Lodge managing to persuade a Helion into burning Sun-Gifts into them; it'd make for a cool story. But in the corebook, no. Helios <i>hates</i> the Uratha, his servitor Choirs vary from disdain to hostility, and giving the reason <i>why</i> he hates them (beyond the not-entirely-accurate but a good enough metaphor &quot;they killed my stepbrother&quot;) is one part of the changes to him in 2nd edition. Once you know, you'll be able to see ways to work around it if you want to.<br /> <br /> Like all spirits, Helios is a self-centered being. He isn't angry at the People for what they did to his sister. He's angry at them for what Father Wolf's death did to <i>him</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T04:31:11-07:00","id":293624,"title":"","content":"Will Helios could be changed to Sol, as Luna could become Moon and Father Wolf being Mother Wolf? In other words - are other Celestials an Firstborn to be changed in gender? I ask, as for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths\">Scandinavian and Roman myths</a> would be more suitable little gender bending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T08:33:44-07:00","id":293748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=293622#post293622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so - and that's unfortunately why they'd be reserved for apocryphal material. I could see an individual Pack or a Lodge managing to persuade a Helion into burning Sun-Gifts into them; it'd make for a cool story. But in the corebook, no. Helios <i>hates</i> the Uratha, his servitor Choirs vary from disdain to hostility, and giving the reason <i>why</i> he hates them (beyond the not-entirely-accurate but a good enough metaphor &quot;they killed my stepbrother&quot;) is one part of the changes to him in 2nd edition. Once you know, you'll be able to see ways to work around it if you want to.<br /> <br /> Like all spirits, Helios is a self-centered being. He isn't angry at the People for what they did to his sister. He's angry at them for what Father Wolf's death did to <i>him</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Helios/Amaterasu/Greatest of Burning Gas Balls <i>always</i> hate the People though? The reasons have shifted(I think for the better from what I'm picking up), but the Uratha have never exactly been It's favorite thing since bread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T09:25:29-07:00","id":293777,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they mention that he doesn't like The People in the old core, but I don't think it's ever been impressed just how deep and impassioned that feeling is for Helios himself. It sounds like Helions way well be up in general antagonist territory, as opposed to most spirits being setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:13:16-07:00","id":293857,"title":"","content":"I was just going off on what Predators mentions in his little blurb. The Searings, Helions hate all the werewolves because of their connection to the nighttime (from Predators) While Helios himself was mad at them to killing his sister's lover. But I've always been fascinated with Helios and his brood...just never was able to explore them in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:45:18-07:00","id":293900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=293622#post293622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an individual Pack or a Lodge managing to persuade a Helion into burning Sun-Gifts into them; it'd make for a cool story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean we still have the brands of renown and gifts as strange symbols on werewolves, visible in the Shadow? It wasn't brought up much outside of a couple books, and most of the art doesn't seem to show it off (the art that does is spectacular). Somewhere a book explained that a werewolf could point to its gift marks as part of the story of its life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:56:20-07:00","id":294110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=293748#post293748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Helios/Amaterasu/Greatest of Burning Gas Balls <i>always</i> hate the People though? The reasons have shifted(I think for the better from what I'm picking up), but the Uratha have never exactly been It's favorite thing since bread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mince words, but doesn't *everything* in the spirit realm hate the uppity predators that show up from the other side of the gauntlet and push them around?<br /> <br /> That is of course discounting spirits powerful enough to have to be palavered with and the favored ones that become totems, but...<br /> <br /> Well hey. I might be conceding the point because 'hate' is too strong of a word? Active malevolence isn't a thing when most spirits are just following their nature, doing what is fundamental to themselves, no? Even 'hate spirits' wouldn't specifically hate the People, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:10:14-07:00","id":294146,"title":"","content":"The implications of most of the &quot;newer&quot; choirs of spirits not having such ingrained antipathy toward the People as the more established courts seemed to be present to make a case for the Uratha as things-that-should-not-be according to Nature As Defined By Shadow in 1e.<br /> <br /> Admittedly it's been a while now since the text was fresh in my mind and things broadly can and confirmedly will change around in 2e, but if anything's going to stain the collective reputation of an entire metaphysical family tree, &quot;the consequences of killing a Celestine&quot; would seem to rank high on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:41:44-07:00","id":294159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=294110#post294110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mince words, but doesn't *everything* in the spirit realm hate the uppity predators that show up from the other side of the gauntlet and push them around?<br /> <br /> That is of course discounting spirits powerful enough to have to be palavered with and the favored ones that become totems, but...<br /> <br /> Well hey. I might be conceding the point because 'hate' is too strong of a word? Active malevolence isn't a thing when most spirits are just following their nature, doing what is fundamental to themselves, no? Even 'hate spirits' wouldn't specifically hate the People, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between hating the local police because you know them to be corrupt and hating the local police because <i>they shot your leg/your's sisters husband</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T16:44:33-07:00","id":294274,"title":"","content":"Rereading blogposts on Forsaken 2ed with my friend, I'm pretty hyped for the game even though I only read tidbits from the first edition so far. I decided to not read further 1ed and just wait for 2ed to get fresh start, thankfully I have other readings to kill the time. And Grisaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:17:34-07:00","id":294289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=294274#post294274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading blogposts on Forsaken 2ed with my friend, I'm pretty hyped for the game even though I only read tidbits from the first edition so far. I decided to not read further 1ed and just wait for 2ed to get fresh start, thankfully I have other readings to kill the time. And Grisaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably for the best. The new corebook is gonna be independent anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:44:55-07:00","id":294299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=294159#post294159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between hating the local police because you know them to be corrupt and hating the local police because <i>they shot your leg/your's sisters husband</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I kind of forgot spirits would still know about that kind of thing. Rather a good point, that whole 'you killed Wolf' thing. It has always seemed like a hard thing to make an issue for a PC who clearly has no guilt for it and is probably still trying to do right by Papa to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:51:40-07:00","id":294323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=294299#post294299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I kind of forgot spirits would still know about that kind of thing. Rather a good point, that whole 'you killed Wolf' thing. It has always seemed like a hard thing to make an issue for a PC who clearly has no guilt for it and is probably still trying to do right by Papa to keep in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine a lot of the street level spirits don't remember-but since we're talking about Amaterasu/Tezcatlipoca, it applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T18:38:39-07:00","id":294396,"title":"","content":"From what Mr. Brookshaw said it's not the affront of killing Father Wolf that caused Helios to hate the Uratha, but what the death caused to happen to Helios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T05:24:58-07:00","id":294722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theon